<%@ include file="/fragments/header.jspf" %><section class="form-page"><%@ include file="/fragments/admin-nav.jspf" %><h2>The Advanced Java lab.</h2><p class="muted">Isolated syllabus demonstrations. The store keeps its business logic in services and database queries in the JDBC DAO layer.</p><div class="lab-grid"><a class="panel" href="${ctx}/demo/jsp"><h3>JSP lifecycle & syntax ↗</h3><p>Declarations, scriptlets, expressions, comments, ServletConfig and JNDI.</p></a><a class="panel" href="${ctx}/demo/sql"><h3>JSTL SQL ↗</h3><p>A read-only category query on an isolated in-memory teaching database.</p></a><a class="panel" href="${ctx}/demo/xml"><h3>JSTL XML ↗</h3><p>Parse a local XML product feed and traverse it using XPath.</p></a></div><div class="panel"><h3>Internationalization, EL, tag files & functions</h3><p>Locale: <c:out value="${empty sessionScope.lang ? 'en' : sessionScope.lang}"/> · Active sessions: ${applicationScope.activeSessions.get()} · Application: ${applicationScope.appName}</p><p>JSTL function: <code>fn:toUpperCase</code> → ${fn:toUpperCase('ShopSphere')}</p><p>Reusable rating tag: <shop:rating value="${4}"/></p><a class="text-link" href="${ctx}/?lang=hi">Hindi storefront ↗</a></div><div class="panel"><h3>Desktop, networking and distributed services</h3><p>Use the commands in the setup guide to launch Swing administration, the socket inventory server/client, and the RMI registry/service/client. All share the same JDBC database. The socket protocol returns serialized Product objects.</p><pre>./scripts/run.sh com.shopsphere.swing.AdminApp
./scripts/run.sh com.shopsphere.network.InventoryServer
./scripts/run.sh com.shopsphere.network.InventoryClient GET_PRODUCT 1
./scripts/run.sh com.shopsphere.rmi.InventoryRmiServer
./scripts/run.sh com.shopsphere.rmi.InventoryRmiClient 1</pre></div><div class="panel"><h3>Applets: historical demonstration</h3><p>Applets executed in browser plugins and used init, start, stop and destroy lifecycle callbacks. Modern browsers do not support the Java plugin. The optional historical source is in docs/legacy; it is excluded from this Java 17 build. Its working modern equivalent is the Swing administration window.</p></div></section><%@ include file="/fragments/footer.jspf" %>
